From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 17:13:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(allwinner): A733: apply Cortex-A76 erratum 3888013

Cortex-A76 erratum 3888013 (Programmer Cat B, present in r0p0-r4p1,
open; SDEN-885749), "Loads issued to Non-Cacheable or Device GRE memory
can violate ordering requirements". A load to a Non-cacheable or
Device-GRE line, then something that orders a younger load after it (an
address dependency through a page-table update, a modification of
executed instructions, or a load-acquire followed by a non-temporal
load), then a younger load to the same line: under specific timing the
younger load returns the stale data the first one brought in. The A733's
A76 cores are r4p1. Non-cacheable memory is what Linux maps for
DMA-coherent buffers and write-combined framebuffers.

Workaround: the reset handler sets CPUACTLR2_EL1[22], which disables
linking several Non-cacheable or Device-GRE loads to one read request
for a line. Arm warns that this "might have a significant performance
impact to Non-cacheable and Device GRE read bandwidth for streaming
scenarios".

Its own patch, so the cost can be measured with and without it on the
same chain. Measured on the A733 (2026-09-26): -51 % Non-cacheable read
bandwidth (ldp) and -34 % (memcpy) on the A76 cores, A55 cores and
cached memory unchanged. Decision: it stays on.

The vendor BL31 is a blob (v2.5) built years before the workaround
existed upstream; it very probably does not apply it.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
 plat/allwinner/sun60i_a733/platform.mk | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/plat/allwinner/sun60i_a733/platform.mk b/plat/allwinner/sun60i_a733/platform.mk
index a18b4cd64..bb7627ba5 100644
--- a/plat/allwinner/sun60i_a733/platform.mk
+++ b/plat/allwinner/sun60i_a733/platform.mk
@@ -88,6 +88,16 @@ ERRATA_A76_2743102		:=	1
 ERRATA_A76_2356586		:=	1
 WORKAROUND_CVE_2025_10263	:=	1
 
+# Cortex-A76 erratum 3888013 (Cat B, r0p0-r4p1, open): a younger load to a
+# Non-cacheable or Device-GRE line can return stale data brought in by an
+# older load to the same line, across an address dependency, an instruction
+# modification or a load-acquire. The reset handler sets CPUACTLR2_EL1[22],
+# so the core no longer links several such loads to one read request. Arm
+# warns of a significant Non-cacheable / Device-GRE read bandwidth loss for
+# streaming; measured on the A733: -51 % (ldp) and -34 % (memcpy)
+# Non-cacheable read bandwidth on the A76 cores.
+ERRATA_A76_3888013		:=	1
+
 USE_COHERENT_MEM		:=	0
 WARMBOOT_ENABLE_DCACHE_EARLY	:=	1
 HW_ASSISTED_COHERENCY		:=	1
